# clean-my-mac

Invoke: `/clean-my-mac` or natural language: "clean my Mac", "free up space", "my Mac is full", "storage is full"

## Phases (in order — never skip)
- Phase -1: Profile user — active tools, backup status, what to protect
- Phase 0: Analyze disk — run `scripts/analyze_storage.sh`, zero deletions
- Phase 1: Safe caches & logs (LOW risk)
- Phase 2: Developer tools — Homebrew, Xcode, Node, Python, Flutter (LOW–MED)
- Phase 3: Docker cleanup (MEDIUM)
- Phase 4: AI model files — list only, never auto-delete (HIGH)
- Phase 5: Time Machine snapshots — requires confirmed backup (MEDIUM)
- Phase 6: Large file review — user decides (USER-DECIDES)
- Phase 7: iCloud optimization — guidance only

## Critical Rules
- Profile → Analyze → Per-phase confirm → Dry-run → Execute
- Show consequence warnings (not just confirms) for tools in active_tools
- NEVER auto-delete ~/Downloads, ~/Documents, ~/Desktop
- Block Phase 5 if has_backup is no or unknown
- Check `config/protected_paths.txt` before every deletion
- Scripts live at `$SKILL_DIR/scripts/` — always use `bash "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/<name>.sh"`
